#: ../../api/eaas.rst:8
msgid ""
"Emulation-as-a-Service exposes a number of RESTful API endpoints users "
"can employ with an API client (including ``curl`` or any other HTTP "
"request tooling) to get information and interact with the resources "
"present in an EaaSI node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:10
msgid "The EaaS/EaaSI API can be useful to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:12
msgid "query and gather metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:13
msgid "interact with the experimental \"UVI\"; see :ref:`uvi`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:14
msgid ""
"control and perform resource exchange between EaaSI nodes via OAI-PMH (it"
" is recommended to interact with OAI-PMH endpoints via the EaaSI UI's "
"built-in functionality, see :ref:`oaipmh` and :ref:`oai-pmh_management`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:17
msgid "Authentication and Access Tokens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:19
msgid ""
"EaaS's public API can return information about Environments and Software "
"present in a specified EaaSI node. Users with an account in that node can"
" query the API based on their unique user context (for example, to "
"receive metadata about Private Environments or imported Software "
"resources) by obtaining an access token from EaaSI's `Keycloak "
"<https://www.keycloak.org/>`_ authentication module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:23
msgid ""
"If no access token/user context is provided, GET requests to the public "
"API may still return metadata on a node's published/public resources "
"(Public Environments)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:25
msgid ""
"Users with an EaaSI account can acquire an access token from their node "
"by sending a POST request to "
"``https://[eaasi.domain]/auth/realms/master/protocol/openid-"
"connect/token``, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:37
msgid ""
"Being sure to replace all information in ``[]`` with the appropriate "
"values/credentials. Tokens are valid for an hour by default, after which "
"they must be regenerated or refreshed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/eaas.rst:39
msgid ""
"A valid request should receive an `OAuth 2.0 access token response "
"<https://www.oauth.com/oauth2-servers/access-tokens/access-token-"
"response/>`_. The received ``access_token`` property value can then be "
"provided in the header of subsequent requests to the EaaS API, for "
"example:"
msgstr ""

